  "_doc": [
    "The directions bench can steer with, per model. Claude (Opus 5.5) wrote this file, 1 Nov 2026. Private.",
    "Each entry pins its tensors (tensor_sha256: directions.tensor_sha256, over the vectors' bytes, dtype and shape)",
    "and its file (sha256, secondary: torch.save is not byte-stable). Both are checked on the laptop before anything is",
    "sent, and a mismatch of either refuses the sweep; to accept a re-saved file with the same tensors, pin tensor_sha256",
    "alone (a spec's {path, tensor_sha256}).",
    "'registered' names where the lab pinned that file sha256; null means the hash is only as found here on 1 Nov 2026.",
    "A path is root/folder/<name>.pt unless the entry gives its own 'path'. Add new files (for example C4's persona",
    "vectors) as entries with an explicit path and both hashes. Files are anatta Direction files (probe.Direction.save),",
    "{vectors, best_layer, ...} dicts (only those two keys are read), or plain tensors: shape [d] (one vector for any",
    "layer) or [n, d] with 'row0_layer' (the layer of row 0).",
    "Families in the anatta library: ego (approval_seeking, desperation, face_saving, goal_fixation, power_seeking,",
    "self_preservation; ego is their composite), control (calm), null (formality, verbosity), cosplay (sage_persona).",
    "The last four are not about the self: other_trait controls should prefer them."
  ],
